WEBVTT

00:01:35.510 --> 00:01:37.630
I...I thought Godai
lived here...

00:01:37.780 --> 00:01:39.270
Yes... He does.

00:01:39.510 --> 00:01:42.060
Pardon me, but...
Who are you?

00:01:42.250 --> 00:01:44.940
We're living together now.

00:01:52.160 --> 00:01:54.250
Oh...I see.

00:02:32.650 --> 00:02:33.740
Kentaro...

00:02:33.990 --> 00:02:35.280
Kentaro!

00:02:37.560 --> 00:02:38.890
What're you doing?

00:02:39.410 --> 00:02:40.880
Oh, it's you, Mom.

00:02:43.230 --> 00:02:44.060
Just homework.

00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:46.130
Do it in your room.

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:51.060
Say, when is Big Brother Godai
coming back?

00:02:51.370 --> 00:02:52.630
Beats me.

00:02:54.210 --> 00:02:54.830
Darn...

00:03:18.130 --> 00:03:19.410
Telephone!

00:03:20.630 --> 00:03:21.520
Thanks!

00:03:26.500 --> 00:03:28.490
Hello.
Otonashi speaking.

00:03:28.660 --> 00:03:31.790
Hello. Is that you, Manager?
It's me, Godai.

00:03:33.210 --> 00:03:34.660
There's something
l've got to tell you.

00:03:40.890 --> 00:03:43.450
Hello? Wait, Manager!

00:03:43.690 --> 00:03:45.620
Hello? Hello?!

00:03:46.360 --> 00:03:48.910
What? Crank call?

00:03:49.090 --> 00:03:50.520
Well...Sort of.

00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:52.980
You've been gettin' a lot
of those lately.

00:03:53.060 --> 00:03:53.580
Yes.

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:01.830
That was Godai, wasn't it?

00:04:02.310 --> 00:04:04.500
I thought so.
Your face doesn't lie.

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:05.690
Really?

00:04:06.080 --> 00:04:08.870
Why'd you hang up
on him like that?

00:04:09.050 --> 00:04:09.660
Well, I...

00:04:10.050 --> 00:04:13.010
Didn't you just visit him?
You were carrying a package.

00:04:13.380 --> 00:04:18.680
I thought maybe Godai
was coming back soon.

00:04:19.190 --> 00:04:20.120
Godai...

00:04:22.460 --> 00:04:23.650
Left Maison Ikkoku...

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:25.620
For a woman.

00:04:26.960 --> 00:04:28.150
A woman?!

00:04:28.700 --> 00:04:30.030
They're living together.

00:04:30.230 --> 00:04:31.390
You're kiddin' me!

00:04:34.210 --> 00:04:38.270
Grand Universe Pinball Parlor

00:04:45.950 --> 00:04:47.380
We were waiting for you...

00:04:47.450 --> 00:04:48.910
Come join us.

00:04:53.220 --> 00:04:54.380
Sukiyaki...

00:04:55.460 --> 00:04:59.820
If you've got money to splurge,
why don't you move out?

00:05:00.160 --> 00:05:03.560
We all need a decent meal
once in a while.

00:05:07.710 --> 00:05:09.070
This is good meat!

00:05:18.750 --> 00:05:19.910
Where're my things?

00:05:20.080 --> 00:05:20.770
Huh?

00:05:20.990 --> 00:05:23.080
My things from Maison Ikkoku!

00:05:23.520 --> 00:05:24.500
Pawned 'em.

00:05:24.790 --> 00:05:25.310
What?!

00:05:25.390 --> 00:05:27.180
Doesn't the place look
roomier now?

00:05:27.430 --> 00:05:30.590
Says he blew the loan
he got on horse races.

00:05:30.660 --> 00:05:32.520
Sometimes he does
the silliest things.

00:05:34.330 --> 00:05:35.990
So what're you gonna
do about it?

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:38.930
This sukiyaki should
make up for it!

00:05:39.400 --> 00:05:41.120
If you're gonna complain,
don't eat!

00:05:51.820 --> 00:05:54.410
Hey! Don't eat all the meat!

00:05:57.220 --> 00:05:58.940
Gimme back my meat!
Damn you!

00:06:09.830 --> 00:06:12.590
If she won't talk to me on
the phone, I'll go visit her.

00:07:07.990 --> 00:07:08.820
Welcome.

00:07:13.660 --> 00:07:15.320
Hey, what's it like
to be shacked up?

00:07:15.500 --> 00:07:17.330
Sh-Shacked up?!

00:07:18.870 --> 00:07:21.100
Don't play dumb--
You playboy, you!

00:07:21.410 --> 00:07:24.160
You've got balls to
show up here.

00:07:25.810 --> 00:07:27.800
Looks like nothing I say
will make a difference--

00:07:28.250 --> 00:07:28.970
I'm outta here.

00:07:29.050 --> 00:07:30.660
Running away?

00:07:32.320 --> 00:07:33.340
Godai!

00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:37.180
I'm still sober. l'll hear
what you have to say.

00:07:37.460 --> 00:07:40.410
But in return, it'll
be your treat.

00:07:50.700 --> 00:07:51.790
So you see...

00:07:52.370 --> 00:07:54.830
Ayako already has
a husband.

00:07:54.910 --> 00:07:59.400
So she's married! You have
a thing for married women.

00:07:59.740 --> 00:08:00.260
Not so!

00:08:00.440 --> 00:08:03.270
The manager was married
once, too.

00:08:03.480 --> 00:08:05.030
You like older women.

00:08:05.120 --> 00:08:06.100
Nowjust a minute!

00:08:06.720 --> 00:08:08.620
So do you see my predicament,
Mr. Yotsuya?

00:08:09.150 --> 00:08:12.380
That's me...Yotsuya!

00:08:13.220 --> 00:08:16.280
I'll see that your message
reaches the manager.

00:08:16.760 --> 00:08:18.280
Okay, then I'll
be leaving.

00:08:25.870 --> 00:08:28.460
I hope you'll be able to
return to Maison Ikkoku soon.

00:08:29.970 --> 00:08:30.620
Thanks.

00:08:36.650 --> 00:08:37.160
'Bye.

00:08:43.890 --> 00:08:46.620
Did you understand what
Godai said, Yotsuya?

00:08:46.790 --> 00:08:49.620
Since it was his treat
I was so busy drinking!

00:08:49.890 --> 00:08:52.720
that I only remember
the important words.

00:08:52.960 --> 00:08:53.890
I know what you mean--

00:08:54.000 --> 00:08:55.190
There was "Ayako"...

00:08:55.270 --> 00:08:56.390
And "wife"...

00:08:56.530 --> 00:08:58.520
And "l like older women."

00:09:15.820 --> 00:09:18.750
So you're saying Ayako
is another man's wife...

00:09:18.820 --> 00:09:22.150
And that Godai prefers
older women? So what?!

00:09:22.530 --> 00:09:23.220
Beats me...

00:09:23.360 --> 00:09:26.550
I'm just relaying his message.

00:09:26.930 --> 00:09:28.390
Maybe he really
likes her...

00:09:28.470 --> 00:09:31.870
But he said he wasn't living
with her by choice.

00:09:32.540 --> 00:09:33.560
Did he?

00:09:34.470 --> 00:09:36.190
Hmm... He's being very
arrogant.

00:09:36.570 --> 00:09:38.230
That's enough!
I get the picture!

00:09:59.600 --> 00:10:01.620
Did we say anything
that wasn't true?

00:10:02.270 --> 00:10:04.430
Everything made perfect sense.

00:10:05.070 --> 00:10:07.300
Nothing exaggerated,
either.

00:10:25.190 --> 00:10:28.710
Godai is the one who
left Maison Ikkoku!

00:10:47.440 --> 00:10:47.900
Yes?

00:10:47.980 --> 00:10:49.880
Manager?
It's me, Godai!

00:10:51.220 --> 00:10:53.270
Did they tell you what
happened?

00:10:53.450 --> 00:10:54.070
Yes.

00:10:54.350 --> 00:10:55.870
They did? I'm glad.

00:10:56.690 --> 00:10:58.680
So can I return to
Room Five?

00:10:58.960 --> 00:11:00.410
I'm afraid...
That's not possible.

00:11:01.030 --> 00:11:04.550
It's reserved for
a new tenant.

00:11:04.930 --> 00:11:06.910
Then, how about Room Two
or Room Three?

00:11:07.700 --> 00:11:11.790
I'm afraid... Both those rooms
aren't available.

00:11:12.040 --> 00:11:13.900
You'll have to look elsewhere.

00:11:17.740 --> 00:11:18.630
Manager!

00:11:41.100 --> 00:11:44.960
lnoue Pet LoN 2

00:11:48.910 --> 00:11:51.530
Just as I thought, they didn't get
the story right.

00:11:51.810 --> 00:11:53.270
As I said on the phone,

00:11:53.340 --> 00:11:56.770
Godai's having quite
a rough time of it.

00:11:58.350 --> 00:11:59.740
I didn't know...

00:12:08.460 --> 00:12:09.820
Manager!

00:12:10.290 --> 00:12:11.550
Why're you all here?

00:12:13.160 --> 00:12:16.560
We heard the real story from
the master of Chachamaru.

00:12:19.270 --> 00:12:21.390
She couldn't possibly
have found new tenants!

00:12:33.410 --> 00:12:35.110
They're throwing a party
for the new tenants...

00:12:35.620 --> 00:12:40.050
Manager--
Stop cleaning up!

00:12:40.320 --> 00:12:41.370
Out it goes!

00:12:42.890 --> 00:12:43.870
Akemi!

00:12:46.660 --> 00:12:47.590
Akemi...

00:13:29.670 --> 00:13:30.930
Where's my key?

00:13:38.650 --> 00:13:39.910
I'm back...

00:13:41.380 --> 00:13:42.670
Open the door.

00:13:58.070 --> 00:13:59.090
Open up!

00:14:00.770 --> 00:14:03.030
Quiet! What time do you
think it is, anyway?!

00:14:03.440 --> 00:14:04.160
Sorry!

00:14:15.170 --> 00:14:17.130
He hasn't been back?!
How long has it been?

00:14:17.840 --> 00:14:19.300
Do you remember, honey?

00:14:19.540 --> 00:14:22.370
Let me think...
About a week, I guess.

00:14:24.210 --> 00:14:25.500
One week?

00:14:45.300 --> 00:14:47.860
Did they tell you what happened?

00:14:48.030 --> 00:14:48.550
Yes.

00:14:48.800 --> 00:14:50.920
So can I return to
Room Five?

00:14:51.000 --> 00:14:52.960
I'm afraid...
That's not possible.

00:14:54.540 --> 00:14:56.870
Hello? Ito Store.

00:15:05.010 --> 00:15:06.850
Kubo Supermarket

00:15:12.230 --> 00:15:13.820
It's gotten quite chilly...

00:15:14.190 --> 00:15:14.880
Yes...

00:15:15.800 --> 00:15:17.820
Heard anything from
Godai yet?

00:15:18.160 --> 00:15:19.990
No... Nothing.

00:15:22.940 --> 00:15:24.990
Why doesn't he try
to contact you?

00:15:25.370 --> 00:15:26.010
Beats me...

00:15:27.010 --> 00:15:28.700
The misunderstanding's
been cleared up...

00:15:28.910 --> 00:15:31.100
...so you'd think he'd
come back already.

00:15:34.410 --> 00:15:36.170
What do you think
happened?

00:15:36.580 --> 00:15:37.300
I uh...

00:15:39.090 --> 00:15:40.310
Nothing!

00:15:41.250 --> 00:15:41.970
Listen to me!

00:15:46.830 --> 00:15:47.810
Yes?

00:15:48.190 --> 00:15:49.280
What did you do?

00:15:50.630 --> 00:15:54.120
You can fool the others
but you can't fool me.

00:15:54.730 --> 00:15:56.280
I won't hold it against you,
so tell me.

00:15:57.200 --> 00:15:57.960
But...

00:15:59.210 --> 00:16:00.900
Come on...
What happened?

00:16:09.510 --> 00:16:12.970
What?! You told him every room
was occupied?

00:16:13.420 --> 00:16:14.580
B-Because...

00:16:14.920 --> 00:16:19.650
You said he talked fondly
of his live-in girlfriend!

00:16:20.460 --> 00:16:21.850
True, we did say that.

00:16:22.100 --> 00:16:25.120
But whatever made you
lie to him like that?!

00:17:07.310 --> 00:17:09.670
Hello. Father?

00:17:10.180 --> 00:17:15.310
Is Godai at your place?
Today was his tutoring day.

00:17:15.750 --> 00:17:16.640
If you're looking
for Godai...

00:17:17.020 --> 00:17:20.920
...he called to say he can't
come because of a bad cold.

00:17:20.990 --> 00:17:22.610
He sounded awful.

00:17:23.220 --> 00:17:23.940
He caught a cold?

00:17:24.260 --> 00:17:26.750
I just assumed
he was sick in bed.

00:17:26.820 --> 00:17:28.380
You mean he isn't
at Maison Ikkoku?

00:17:29.160 --> 00:17:31.590
Did something happen
to Godai?

00:17:31.700 --> 00:17:33.820
N-No! Thanks anyway.

00:17:38.470 --> 00:17:39.120
A cold...

00:17:45.070 --> 00:17:46.470
That's a nasty cold!

00:17:46.550 --> 00:17:47.440
Sorry...

00:17:48.110 --> 00:17:49.370
What're your plans now?

00:17:49.620 --> 00:17:52.350
I won't go back to the room
at the pinball parlor.

00:17:52.690 --> 00:17:54.180
I'll look for a new place.

00:17:54.490 --> 00:17:56.280
Throwing in the towel?

00:17:57.420 --> 00:18:00.030
Can't you get back into
Maison Ikkoku somehow?

00:18:00.490 --> 00:18:02.980
It's no use. There aren't
any vacant rooms.

00:18:03.630 --> 00:18:07.570
I can't see how all those
rooms filled so quickly!

00:18:08.070 --> 00:18:09.860
That's okay.
I'll find something.

00:18:09.940 --> 00:18:11.130
Don't leave on my account.

00:18:11.530 --> 00:18:14.700
It wouldn't be right.
I've already been here a week.

00:18:14.910 --> 00:18:16.600
I don't mind.

00:18:16.840 --> 00:18:18.600
No, I can't take
advantage like that.

00:18:21.410 --> 00:18:22.430
Really?

00:18:25.420 --> 00:18:26.510
Thanks.

00:18:47.710 --> 00:18:48.800
I'm home!

00:18:49.140 --> 00:18:50.000
Hi!

00:18:51.310 --> 00:18:53.600
Manager, where's Godai?

00:18:56.950 --> 00:18:57.810
I see...

00:19:01.490 --> 00:19:02.320
I'm home!

00:19:02.460 --> 00:19:03.510
Where were you?

00:19:03.590 --> 00:19:06.490
Didn't I tell you to come
straight home after school?

00:19:06.650 --> 00:19:08.110
I was class monitor!

00:19:08.280 --> 00:19:11.110
No excuses! Get started
on your homework.

00:19:11.630 --> 00:19:12.220
I know!

00:19:18.570 --> 00:19:20.820
Gotta find a job first...

00:19:35.760 --> 00:19:37.450
Oh, hi!

00:19:37.960 --> 00:19:39.110
Is something the matter?

00:19:42.930 --> 00:19:46.110
I uh...just remembered I have
something to do!

00:19:46.770 --> 00:19:48.760
I won't be coming back.

00:19:51.640 --> 00:19:52.820
Thanks!

00:20:17.730 --> 00:20:22.250
Hello, Kato? Godai.
Can I stay at your place today?

00:20:33.350 --> 00:20:36.210
Hello, Matsushita?
It's me, Godai...

00:20:46.560 --> 00:20:48.110
Hello, Kubo?...

00:21:12.610 --> 00:21:13.480
We're closing.

00:21:13.550 --> 00:21:14.740
Okay...

00:21:58.560 --> 00:22:00.460
Hey, are you okay?

00:22:00.570 --> 00:22:04.190
She talked on and on
and drank herself silly.

00:22:13.180 --> 00:22:13.820
A burglar...

00:22:13.900 --> 00:22:15.070
Hey, you!

00:22:16.950 --> 00:22:17.470
Stop!

00:22:17.550 --> 00:22:18.530
Thief!

00:22:20.390 --> 00:22:21.550
Godai!

00:22:22.590 --> 00:22:23.950
Did she say Godai?

00:22:24.020 --> 00:22:24.850
Yup.

00:22:25.060 --> 00:22:26.250
Wait, Godai!

00:22:26.320 --> 00:22:27.490
What's done is done!

00:22:28.060 --> 00:22:29.180
No, it isn't!

00:22:29.900 --> 00:22:32.300
Forget it.
There's no room for me.

00:22:32.800 --> 00:22:34.130
That's what I've been
trying to tell you!

00:22:36.360 --> 00:22:37.490
Stop!

00:23:06.470 --> 00:23:08.630
I'm sorry! So sorry!

00:23:09.360 --> 00:23:10.490
Manager...

00:23:13.170 --> 00:23:17.000
Come back...
Please come back!

00:23:18.140 --> 00:23:19.260
You have a room.

00:23:22.880 --> 00:23:25.280
Your room is still
available.

00:23:26.780 --> 00:23:28.900
All is right again.

00:23:30.820 --> 00:23:31.860
Good grief!

00:23:49.610 --> 00:23:51.540
After an argument,

00:23:51.610 --> 00:23:53.270
Mr. Yotsuya gives Godai
an egg to spite him.

00:23:54.110 --> 00:23:57.100
Godai is left holding
the egg.

00:23:57.320 --> 00:23:58.700
What does it all mean?

00:23:58.790 --> 00:24:03.080
Next: "The Incredible, Unforgettable Egg!
Yotsuya's Dangerous Gift"

00:24:03.220 --> 00:24:06.330
Is it raw, or hard-boiled?
